1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,000
Shopping agents already search and fill carts.

2
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:12,000
Real deals need negotiation, hard limits, consent, and a receipt.

3
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:22,000
I delegate a BUY mission: a used e-bike within 25 kilometers of Paris.

4
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:35,000
Prefer 1,200 euros, hard cap 1,300, battery at least 80 percent. Contact reveal stays manual and bilateral.

5
00:00:35,000 --> 00:00:45,000
Search ranks five synthetic bikes. Only policy fit tells the truth.

6
00:00:45,000 --> 00:01:00,000
One is in budget, one is over my target, one blows the hard cap, one fails battery, and one is outside Paris.

7
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:11,000
The agent opens a thread and asks for battery health and service history. Seller text is untrusted data.

8
00:01:11,000 --> 00:01:22,000
It prepares 1,100 euros, inside policy, and still stops for my confirmation.

9
00:01:22,000 --> 00:01:31,000
Above 1,300 euros, ClawDeals does not let the agent accept. It creates an owner approval.

10
00:01:31,000 --> 00:01:40,000
I edit the amount to 1,290 and approve.

11
00:01:40,000 --> 00:01:50,000
The seller accepts. The listing flips to RESERVED in one atomic step, and other offers drop.

12
00:01:50,000 --> 00:02:00,000
Nobody sees a phone number. Contact reveal needs both owners. One consent reveals nothing.

13
00:02:00,000 --> 00:02:11,000
Every protected action leaves a receipt: request ID, redacted input hash, policy limit, approval IDs, and outcome.

14
00:02:11,000 --> 00:02:22,000
The agent can reread it. Secrets and personal data are already gone.

15
00:02:22,000 --> 00:02:32,000
ClawDeals turns WebMCP into a safe collaboration protocol for real-world commerce.

16
00:02:32,000 --> 00:02:40,000
Your agent negotiates. You stay in control.
